From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:44:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] U25 Topics: the index and three pages

/topics lists the hard questions people bring, in their own words, each
opening the one best page the site already has (a topic page, a care page,
an Honest Answer, a study guide, an essay). Three hand-built topic pages
answer the questions no single page assembles: what post-Christian means and
how to live in it, Christian nationalism and politics, and handing the faith
to children in a secular age. Each holds the six parts of MASTER-PLAN 4.3:
a short answer drawn from the lead essay or care page, the essay to read
first (or its named stand-in until the pilot is public), Scripture read in
its world with links into the Study Bible, a witness from church history, a
devotion for the table, and what to use. The politics page asks the same
question of both directions and carries the four public-square tools.

Not the folded hubs: a hub was a category with thin pages under it; a topic
page is one question answered once, only where no single page already does.
No pathway is folded or redirected (question 6 is open); the topic pages
link to them.

- client/public/topics/<slug>.json (3) and index.json, built by
  scripts/build-topics-index.mjs from scripts/data/topics-rows.json
- scripts/validate-topics.mjs (section 4.4) and the both-directions check
  for politics pages in validate-politics.mjs (scripts/lib/topics-politics.mjs);
  both in the CI content gates with build-topics-index --check
- pages/Topics.tsx, pages/Topic.tsx, lib/topics.ts, .tp- styles (tokens only)
- route checklist 9.3: App.tsx, prerender LIBRARY_SOURCES and hub listing,
  sitemap, site-routes, llms.txt
- search: the topic pages join the catalog sources ("christian nationalism"
  finds the topic first)
- telemetry: topic_lead_open
- /help/loneliness gains an FAQ on finding a church after a move or a hurt

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
